[%# cloud-init network-config v1 for a guest, rendered by
    Provisioner::Recipe::ubuntu.

    Two interfaces: the outbound bridge, which carries the addresses this guest
    is reached at, and the libvirt NAT, which is how the hypervisor finds it
    before those work.

    Matched on MAC rather than on name.  The names below are what each ends up
    called; which card is which is decided by the address, because that is the
    one thing about an interface we choose and the guest cannot disagree with.

    No apostrophes in an Xslate comment: the lexer reads one as opening a
    string and swallows the template as far as the next quote. -%]
---
[% IF !bridge_mac -%]
[%# Nothing here defined this machine, so its MACs and interface names are not
    ours to know: a service assigned them when it created the guest.  There is
    no way to write a config matched on a MAC we were never told, and the
    platform has already addressed the guest -- so say so, which is cloud-init
    for leave the network alone. -%]
network:
  config: disabled
[% ELSE -%]
network:
  version: 1
  config:
    - type: physical
      name: [% bridge_devname | yaml %]
      mac_address: [% bridge_mac | yaml %]
[% IF gateway -%]
      gateway4: [% gateway | yaml %]
[% END -%]
      nameservers:
        search:
          - [% domain | yaml %]
        addresses:
[% FOR resolver IN resolvers -%]
          - [% resolver | yaml %]
[% END -%]
      subnets:
[% IF ips.size() -%]
[% FOR ip IN ips -%]
        - type: static
          address: [% ip | yaml %]
          gateway: [% gateway | yaml %]
          dns_search:
            - [% domain | yaml %]
          dns_nameservers:
[% FOR resolver IN resolvers -%]
            - [% resolver | yaml %]
[% END -%]
[% END -%]
[% ELSE -%]
[%# No addresses configured, so the bridge asks for one the same way the NAT
    side does.  Which is rarely what you want on the outbound side, and is what
    a guest with no ips in its provision.conf gets. -%]
        - type: dhcp
[% END -%]
    - type: physical
      name: [% dhcp_devname | yaml %]
      mac_address: [% nat_mac | yaml %]
      subnets:
        - type: dhcp
[% END -%]
